- How adapt to larger alphabets or different segment metrics?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests classic DP with an additional dimension (at most k intervals) and reconstruction—a common pattern in scheduling optimization problems.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a cardinality constraint (at most k intervals)
- Predecessor p(i) computed via binary search on sorted end times
- DP table with an extra dimension tracking the number of selected intervals
- Backtracking reconstruction to output the chosen jobs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueKJobs(jobs, k) {
  const sorted = jobs.map((j, idx) => ({ ...j, idx })).sort((a, b) => a.end - b.end);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const ends = sorted.map(j => j.end);

  const p = (i) => {
    let lo = 0, hi = i - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
      if (ends[mid] <= sorted[i].start) lo = mid + 1;
      else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return hi;
  };

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const prev = p(i - 1) + 1;
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], dp[prev][t - 1] + sorted[i - 1].value);
    }
  }

  const selected = [];
  let t = k;
  for (let i = n; i > 0 && t > 0; i--) {
    if (dp[i][t] !== dp[i - 1][t]) {
      selected.push(sorted[i - 1]);
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], jobs: selected.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked

This problem tests dynamic programming with turn constraints on grid paths, requiring careful state design and path reconstruction. It evaluates understanding of edge case handling and performance optimization for large inputs.

## Key Concepts

- **4D DP state**: position (i, j), turn count (t), and ending direction (d)
- **Two transition types**: continuing in the same direction versus making a turn
- **Path reconstruction**: using parent pointers or backtracking to retrieve the actual path
- **Time and space trade-offs**: consider optimization for large grids

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxPathWithKTurns(M, k) {
  const n = M.length;
  const m = M[0].length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(null).map(() =>
    Array(m).fill(null).map(() =>
      Array(k + 1).fill(null).map(() => [-1, -1])
    )
  );

  dp[0][0][0][0] = dp[0][0][0][1] = M[0][0];

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        for (let d = 0; d < 2; d++) {
          if (dp[i][j][t][d] < 0) continue;

          if (i + 1 < n) {
            const newD = 1;
            const newT = d === newD ? t : t + 1;
            if (newT <= k) {
              dp[i + 1][j][newT][newD] = Math.max(
                dp[i + 1][j][newT][newD],
                dp[i][j][t][d] + M[i + 1][j]
              );
            }
          }

          if (j + 1 < m) {
            const newD = 0;
            const newT = d === newD ? t : t + 1;
            if (newT <= k) {
              dp[i][j + 1][newT][newD] = Math.max(
                dp[i][j + 1][newT][newD],
                dp[i][j][t][d] + M[i][j + 1]
              );
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return Math.max(dp[n - 1][m - 1][k][0], dp[n - 1][m - 1][k][1]);
}
```

## Complexity

- **Time**: O(n × m × k)
- **Space**: O(n × m × k)
